  "review_findings_fixed": [
    "Reconfirmation cannot repin missing or substituted local sources after unpin/retention; exact verified manifest required",
    "Unpin enumerates every bounded outbox and refuses partial evidence or pending claims at any destination; schedule and backup locks serialize selection, retention and pin release",
    "Quota counts actual partial and orphan storage, includes tar overhead in bounded spool writes, preserves unknown-sized Dolt export overruns, and denies subsequent allocation"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Dolt export quota enforcement is admission plus post-export/verification checkpoints, not a hard filesystem quota. Apparent regular-file bytes exclude allocated-block overhead and filesystem metadata.",
    "Quota scope is owned instance backup and replication-spool directories. External scratch archives are outside policy. No implicit pruning, unpinning, partial cleanup or remote deletion.",
    "Unpin requires local verified evidence and fresh full remote proof for all recorded destinations. Pending or corrupt records remain conservatively pinned. Remote proof establishes current availability only.",
    "Repeated unpin apply safely refuses an already unpinned source; later successful explicit replication repins it after verifying local identity.",
    "Outbox enumeration is bounded to 10000 entries and 64KiB per payload, failing closed instead of truncating.",
    "Native and real-provider network mutations use disposable localhost adapter/replica services. No vendor-specific production deployment.",
    "Formal checks cover production predicates and bounded lifecycle/order models, not entire filesystem, Dolt, HTTP, Git or provider implementations."
  ],
